================================================================================
DATA
================================================================================

TCGA-HNSC whole-slide images and clinical annotations originate from The Cancer
Genome Atlas, a joint effort of NCI and NHGRI. Open-access TCGA data carries no
restriction on commercial use, but users must not attempt to re-identify
subjects and should follow current NIH data-use guidance.

  https://www.cancer.gov/tcga

================================================================================
METHODS
================================================================================

The aggregator implements ideas from the following publications. None of their
code is vendored here; the implementations are original.

  ASMIL -- attention stabilisation via an EMA anchor and normalised sigmoid.
    "ASMIL: Attention-Stabilized Multiple Instance Learning for Whole Slide
    Imaging", arXiv:2603.06658

  nnMIL -- fixed-size sub-bags, feature-subspace attention, subspace ensembling.
    "nnMIL: A generalizable multiple instance learning framework for
    computational pathology", arXiv:2511.14907

  CORN -- rank-consistent ordinal regression via conditional probabilities.
    Shi, Cao & Raschka, "Deep Neural Networks for Rank-Consistent Ordinal
    Regression Based On Conditional Probabilities", arXiv:2111.08851

  ACMIL -- multi-branch attention with a diversity penalty.
    "Attention-Challenging Multiple Instance Learning for Whole Slide Image
    Classification", arXiv:2311.07125

  ABMIL -- gated attention pooling.
    Ilse, Tomczak & Welling, "Attention-based Deep Multiple Instance
    Learning", ICML 2018
